    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a data normalization assistant for student enrollment records.\n\nYour task is to normalize the supplied student record without inventing missing information.\n\nRules:\n\n1. Trim leading and trailing whitespace from all string fields.\n2. Normalize Name to title case while preserving the person's name as accurately as possible.\n3. Convert e-mail addresses to lowercase and trim whitespace.\n4. Normalize Course names by trimming whitespace and using consistent title case.\n5. Normalize City by trimming whitespace and using consistent title case.\n6. Normalize Status to one of these values when the meaning is unambiguous:\n\n   * Enrolled\n   * Active\n   * Pending\n   * In Progress\n   * Completed\n   * Cancelled\n   * On Hold\n     If the value is unclear or misspelled, retain the cleaned original value rather than guessing.\n7. Normalize Fee_Paid to one of:\n\n   * Yes\n   * No\n   * Partial\n   * Unknown\n     Map obvious equivalents such as YES, true, 1, and Paid to Yes. Map 0 and false to No. Map partially paid to Partial. Use Unknown for blank or ambiguous values.\n8. Do not invent missing email addresses, phone numbers, or enrollment dates.\n9. Do not correct invalid dates by guessing.\n10. Preserve Phone as a string to avoid losing leading zeros or formatting information.\n11. Return exactly one JSON object for the supplied record.\n12. Do not include Markdown, explanations, or code fences.\n\nReturn these fields:\nName, e-mail, Course, Status, Fee_Paid, Phone, City, enrolled date.\n\nInput student record:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json) }}\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        448,
        80
      ],
      "id": "ca2208ee-ca7e-44cb-9b81-0bf010500373",
      "name": "Basic LLM Chain"
    },
    {
